      "ply": 10,
      "title": "Opening the centre too early",
      "text": "Playing e5 opens the position while your king is still in the middle. After dxe5 you are a pawn down and have to spend time winning it back. Nxe4 was simpler: you trade White's active knight, and after Qxe4 you can develop calmly with Qd5 and Bf5.",
